        'For most of the twentieth century, rice and wheat dominated Indian plates. Millets such as jowar, bajra and ragi, once the staple food of many regions, came to be seen as "poor people\'s grain". Farmers switched to crops that the market rewarded, and a generation grew up without ever tasting a ragi roti.',
